erty Island from the first movie  Logan builds on the post-credits scene  from x-men apocalypse where we saw dark  suited men from ethics Corp walk into  the Weapon X facility at alkali Lake to  collect various blood samples being  stored there in Logan is a company  called alkali transition which is taken  up the Weapon X program creating new  young mutants like X 23 the name alkali  transition could be a double reference  to both alkali lake were the Weapon X  program started and transition could it  be a nod to Terrigen mists karagin is a  substance from the comics that when it  was released in  the Earth's atmosphere slowly started  killing off mutants and as a curious  parallel in the movie when Vander Rice  explains how alkali transition  distributed gene therapy through soda  and breakfast cereals to almost  eradicate random mutations writers plan  wasn't to exterminate all mutants  however but to eradicate any mutants  that they didn't develop and control  themselves  Rice's virus like gene therapy could  also provide an explanation for why  Logan's mutant healing factor has been  waning by the ways and arises the lead  scientist responsible for creating x-23  just like he is in the comics and in  Logan we also learned that Wolverine was  responsible for killing Rice's father  which also happened in the comics when  he went berserk ordering his escape from  Weapon X and x-men apocalypse when Logan  flips through transition Case Files at  the hotel we see notes revealing some of  the source DNA for the young mutants  including DNA from Jane Paulus aka Logan  which was used for X 23 another case  file reveals that one of the sources of  DNA is Christopher Bradley you appeared  in x-men origins Wolverine was one of  the original team x members Bradley was  able to control electrical devices but  left the team until he was hunted down  by Sabretooth to retrieve his DNA for  the weapon eleven programs in Logan we  find out that Professor X has gone into  hiding and has to take regular  medication to prevent seizures that can  cause catastrophe all around him and at  one point in the movie a radio report  mentions the Westchester incidents which  occurred here previously in which  various mutants were killed Westchester  is the location of the x-mansion and the  heavy implication that Charles  accidentally lost control of his powers  killing many of the x-men this is a nod  to the old man Logan comic storyline  which Logan loosely adapt where it was  Wolverine who accidentally slaughtered  the x-men after being tricked by the  villain Mysterio by the way there are  some cool visual nods to that comic  series such as this shot of Logan  punching a guy all the way through his  skull with his claws and there's another  picture of Hugh Jackman's Logan looking  grizzled and worn with a couple of chest  wounds which is evocative of his look in  old man Logan another comic book series  which heavily influenced the Logan movie  is death of Wolverine in the comic book  series Wolverine also meets his end as  he rescued a group of mutants that are  being experimented on by dr. Cornelius  Atheneum  of the Weapon X program and in Logan the  young mutants hideout is a location  called Eden a name that has echoes as a  paradise face that loathe and refuse  them from in death of Wolverine death of  Wolverine also features a Logan whose  healing factor has stopped working  properly and where Wolverine uses a  serum on himself at the end of the movie  it's a nod to how he gave the mutants he  rescued in the comics a regenerative  serum by the way some of the mutants at  Logan and x-23 meet up with us  Eden hint towards possible future  x-force members says Rick tore an  original x-force member in the comics  with extremely powerful seismic  abilities which in the movie at one  point he uses against x24 and another  young mutant gideon is an x-force mutant  villain in the comics  although Wolverines comic book Canary  costume was teased in the alternate  ending to James Mangold's movie The  Wolverine we don't actually get to see  it in Logan where it properly would have  felt out of place in terms of the tone  set by the movie it's got a cool Easter  egg to the costume though at the very  end of the movie during Logan's funeral  when one of the mutant children is  holding a Wolverine toy dressed in the  canary costume the costume also appears  earlier via the x-men comics that Logan  finds Laura is reading the x-men comics  that Laura was reading were made  especially for the movie however one of  the issue numbers is 132 which could  point the real comic book uncanny x-men  number 132 where Wolverine meets Don  appeared for the first time as they  fight in that comic Wolverine discovers  Donald Pierce's cybernetic arm which of  course he also has in the Logan movie  and Logan's comments as he flips through  the comics or an interesting bit of  commentary on the status of superheroes  in this part of the x-men universe when  Logan says that maybe a quarter of it  happened and not like this he's  commenting on how he's tired of heroes  being mythologized and turned into  celebrities whose stories are constantly  retold and distorted and it could also  be a little sideswipe at the x-men movie  franchise and how it's become known for  messing around with the timelines which  end up wiping away the events of the  whole movie trilogy and introducing new  continuity problems at the same time  nevertheless Logan still includes a  little homage to how Fox like to  sprinkle X symbols into the x-men movies  when Laura turns across and Wolverines  grave onto its side so it resembles  x-man goals Logan also channels several  non superhero movies a couple a  particular note of the road movie Little  Miss Sunshine starring Abigail Breslin  and the 1953 Western Shane's which  features a gunslinger hero who wants to  leave his past behind  Shane gets various shout outs in the  movie and it's clear that Mangal feels a  